    "notes": "Inspected all 60 current near/repeated base-color swatches and the focused raw basalt/sandstone sheet. Basalt is finely granular and nondirectional; sandstone has restrained horizontal sediment grain. They contain no block seams and preserve their low-contrast grain over3×3 repeats. ETFE remains smooth white film, weathered limestone is visibly mottled, and painted timber retains distinct course patterns. PBR normals and metric UV fit are separately reviewed on each model. The two additional canonical cutout/bronze swatches were inspected separately; previous60 graphs remain byte-identical. The new square-hole graph also passed all32 Mordovia portable/shared model views, including close openings and distant mip behavior. Cast bronze contains fine continuous patination without sheet joints. Round-cutout near/repeated swatch inspected: circular apertures, neutral tintable painted sheet, no dark painted substitute for alpha holes. Its concrete model UV/mip review belongs to Rostec Arena QA. Inspected round-open-cutout.png near/repeated swatch: neutral painted web remains continuous between large transparent circular apertures. Hole diameter is reconstructed within a published30–60% range; actual facade UV/mip review belongs to Cayan model QA. Expanded-diamond near/repeated swatch inspected: transparent staggered diamond apertures join without texture-border seams and retain continuous diagonal metal webs. The square source UV swatch stretches to3:1 on metric model UVs. The measured56% opening comes from the SBP Warsaw maintenance manual;0.12×0.04m physical repeat is a photograph reconstruction. Model-scale UV and mip behavior require the Warsaw model review."
  },
  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "maximum",
    "status": "pending",
    "notes": "These are deterministic 256² procedural surfaces, not scans. Swatches show base color only. Tangent normals, metric orientation, physically scaled repeats and actual lighting require per-model rendered review. New painted shingles have regular widths; canvas yarn detail and granite microstructure are limited by the texture resolution. Unique local wear, murals and facade art remain model-specific."
  },
